{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786209976,"nonce":"bTsOw9lXS9AQo62BmuuEsnygr5g=","title":"**What is wrong.** The SolidJS app in `web/` has only ever been driven against a","message":"mock server (`scratchpad/mock.mjs` in the build session). Until `e776716` the SSE\nstream sent no `Content-Type: text/event-stream` at all — the conformance audit\nproved it on the wire:\n\n```\nGET /api/v1/stream?resources=alerts\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nVary: Origin\nX-Request-Id: …\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\n\n: ping\n```\n\n\"All four declared headers are absent on the wire… a browser `EventSource`\n**rejects** a response whose Content-Type is not `text/event-stream` and fires\n`onerror`\" (`review-conformance.md` C-8). The header ordering bug is fixed and\ncovered by `internal/platform/httpx/sse_test.go`, but no browser has ever held a\nlive stream open against this server.\n\n**Why it matters.** Live updating is the reason the UI exists rather than a\nGrafana panel; ADR 0010 (SSE with durable resume) is entirely unexercised. Resume\nafter reconnect, the `Last-Event-ID` cursor, interest filters, and the app's\nreducer for each event type are all unproven. A user who leaves the alert list\nopen is the normal case, and today nobody knows what they see.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/api/`, `web/src/features/`, `internal/streaming/`,\n`internal/platform/httpx/sse.go`, ADR 0010.\n\n**Done when.** The UI is run against `go run ./cmd/oto serve` with a real\nPostgres: login, alert list, alert detail, ack, snooze, settings and the sources\nscreen all work; an alert ingested by webhook appears in an open list without a\nrefresh; killing and restoring the connection resumes without duplicate or lost\nevents. Findings are fixed, and the flow is captured as a test or a scripted\ncheck so it does not silently rot again.","files":null}]}